{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"chronological","type":"text","text":"# Chronological Assumption\n\n**Single point of failure.**\n\nThe assumption that biblical texts\npreserve pre-exilic religious data\nin recoverable form.\n\n**Defend this** → graph withstands\nHeiser, Tigay, and Kaufmann.\n\n**Lose it** → ~59% of claims lose\ntheir evidential foundation.\n\nThe graph's entire evolutionary\nnarrative depends on this.","x":1920,"y":80,"width":340,"height":440,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"schmid","type":"text","text":"# Schmid\n## Pentateuch = Persian-Period; No Pre-Exilic Windows\n\n**Survival: 41%**\nThreatens 5 full + 8 partial hinges | ~112 claims\n\n**Mechanism:** Methodological undercutting\nDoes not dispute individual claims — denies\nthe evidence base has pre-exilic value.\nEliminates the chronological framework\nthat the entire graph depends on.\n\n**What breaks:** J/E/D/P as evolutionary\ntimeline. Source criticism survives as\nliterary analysis but cannot serve as\nchronological framework.\n\n**Minimum revision:** The evolutionary\nnarrative becomes a hypothesis about\na 500-year textual dark age, not a\ndocumented sequence.","x":1240,"y":-580,"width":380,"height":580,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"survivor","type":"text","text":"# What Survives Everything\n\nEvidence independent of biblical dating.\nNo counter-position can eliminate these:\n\n- **Ugaritic texts** — 14th-13th c. BCE\n  securely dated tablets\n- **Archaeology** — Kuntillet Ajrud,\n  Khirbet el-Qom, pillar figurines,\n  cult stands (independently dated)\n- **Epigraphy / Onomastics** — 8th-6th c.\n  Hebrew inscriptions (Tigay's data)\n- **Merneptah Stele** — c. 1207 BCE\n  \"Israel\" attested regardless of\n  biblical dating\n- **Comparative ANE** — Mesopotamian,\n  Egyptian, Ugaritic parallels\n  (independent textual corpora)\n\nThese 5 clusters form the\narchaeologically-anchored core.\n\n[[notes/synthesis/capstone-what-does-this-mean]]","x":1160,"y":775,"width":420,"height":580,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"threat-tiers","type":"text","text":"# Threat Tiers\n\n## Tier 1 — Nuclear\n**Schmid (41% survival)**\nEliminates chronological framework.\nSingle point of failure: biblical texts\nas pre-exilic evidence.\n\n## Tier 2 — Paradigm\n**Kaufmann (58% survival)**\nFlips graph polarity. Evidence stays,\nstory inverts. Revolution replaces\nevolution.\n\n## Tier 3 — Local\n**Heiser (72%) · Tigay (85%)**\nDamage specific hinge claims.\nGraph absorbs through reinterpretation.\nOverall framework intact.","x":-1080,"y":-1187,"width":340,"height":607,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"tigay","type":"text","text":"# Tigay\n## 94%+ Onomastic Evidence = Yahwistic Dominance\n\n**Survival: 85%**\nThreatens 2 hinges | ~28 claims\n\n**Mechanism:** Narrow empirical challenge\nInscriptions have no editors — cannot\nbe dismissed as elite propaganda.\n\n**Tigay's own caution limits blast radius:**\nNames ≠ monotheism. Consensus absorbs\nhim as evidence for Yahweh-as-chief-god,\nnot Yahweh-as-only-god.\n\n**Real threat:** Tonal — makes \"everywhere\nand always polytheistic\" harder to sustain.\nDever's claim already has 4 contradict edges.","x":-1080,"y":0,"width":360,"height":600,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"kaufmann","type":"text","text":"# Kaufmann\n## Monotheism = Revolution from the Beginning\n\n**Survival: 58%**\nThreatens 4 hinges | ~63 claims\n\n**Mechanism:** Paradigm inversion\nSame data, opposite narrative.\nEvolutionary → Revolutionary.\n\n**Survives:**\n- Ugaritic parallels (as background, not influence)\n- Archaeology (partially; reinterpreted as vestigial)\n- Onomastics (strengthened — Tigay alignment)\n\n**Irony:** Kaufmann IS already in the graph\nas hinges #4, #6, #15, #18. The central fault\nline is Kaufmann vs. the consensus he helped\nbuild — most cited AND most contradicted.","x":-20,"y":775,"width":360,"height":650,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"center","type":"text","text":"# Consensus Graph\n## 715 Active Claims\n\n25 hinge claims identified\n4 counter-positions stress-tested\nBFS cascade analysis (4 levels deep)\n\n**Vulnerability profile:**\n- Chronological assumption = single point of failure\n- Survives Tigay & Heiser structurally\n- Kaufmann flips graph polarity\n- Schmid eliminates evidential foundation\n\n[[notes/synthesis/phase1-hinge-inventory]]\n[[notes/synthesis/phase3-counter-position-stress-tests]]","x":440,"y":0,"width":400,"height":480,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"heiser","type":"text","text":"# Heiser\n## Elyon = Yahweh; Hierarchical Monotheism\n\n**Survival: 72%**\nThreatens 3 hinges | ~47 claims\n\n**Mechanism:** Textual reinterpretation\nDeut 32:8-9 — Elyon as Yahweh-epithet,\nnot a separate deity. The 70 sons are\nsubordinate created beings.\n\n**Survives:**\n- Archaeology (untouched)\n- Ugaritic parallels (independent)\n- Divine embodiment claims\n- Epigraphic onomastics\n- Sociological dynamics\n\n**Second-order:** Relabeling, not demolition.\nDivine council survives — reinterpreted\nas hierarchical monotheism.","x":460,"y":-760,"width":360,"height":630,"color":"2"}
	],
